  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Indiana received $84M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The state logged 2,023 awards with an average award size of $41.5K, and obligations fell 98.3% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying activity with $52.8M in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration with $8.8M and the Department of Justice with $8.4M. ROCHE DIAGNOSTICS CORPORATION was the top vendor with $19.4M, and LIFE SCIENCE LOGISTICS LLC and AFTER ACTION MEDICAL AND DENTAL SUPPLY, LLC followed with $7M and $4.3M respectively. Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $16M, with General Warehousing and Storage at $7M and Special Needs Transportation at $6.5M. Historical context shows larger prior fiscal years: FY22 obligations were $8.5B, FY23 were $6.7B, FY24 were $6.3B, FY25 were $8.1B, and FY26 were $5B. Current-year totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are awarding most of the contracts in Indiana?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $52.8M in Indiana, making it the largest buying agency for FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $8.8M and the Department of Justice obligated $8.4M. The Department of Homeland Security and NASA obligated $7.2M and $2.7M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and industries receiving federal dollars in Indiana?",
        "body": "ROCHE DIAGNOSTICS CORPORATION received $19.4M in obligations, making it the top vendor in FY2027 to date. LIFE SCIENCE LOGISTICS LLC and AFTER ACTION MEDICAL AND DENTAL SUPPLY, LLC received $7M and $4.3M respectively. Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing received $16M in obligations, followed by General Warehousing and Storage with $7M and Special Needs Transportation with $6.5M."
      }
